    "difficulty": "EASY",
    "stem": "Expand \\(\\left(x^{2}+\\dfrac{3}{x}\\right)^{4}\\), \\(x \\neq 0\\).",
    "solution": "By using binomial theorem, we have\n\n\\(\\left(x^{2}+\\dfrac{3}{x}\\right)^{4} = {}^{4}C_{0}(x^{2})^{4} + {}^{4}C_{1}(x^{2})^{3}\\left(\\dfrac{3}{x}\\right) + {}^{4}C_{2}(x^{2})^{2}\\left(\\dfrac{3}{x}\\right)^{2} + {}^{4}C_{3}(x^{2})\\left(\\dfrac{3}{x}\\right)^{3} + {}^{4}C_{4}\\left(\\dfrac{3}{x}\\right)^{4}\\)\n\n\\(= x^{8} + 4 \\cdot x^{6} \\cdot \\dfrac{3}{x} + 6 \\cdot x^{4} \\cdot \\dfrac{9}{x^{2}} + 4 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot \\dfrac{27}{x^{3}} + \\dfrac{81}{x^{4}}\\)\n\n\\(= x^{8} + 12x^{5} + 54x^{2} + \\dfrac{108}{x} + \\dfrac{81}{x^{4}}\\)."
  },
  {
